# Sentry capture-has-init allowlist baseline (FOLLOW-759).
#
# CONSUMER of the allowlist inventory printed by
# scripts/check-sentry-capture-has-init.sh. Each entry is:
#
#   <path relative to the repo root> (<N> occurrence(s))
#
# i.e. one line per SCANNED file that carries at least one
# `# sentry-init-guard: allowlisted` annotation, with how many it carries.
# Per-file counts rather than file:line, deliberately: line numbers churn on
# every unrelated edit above an annotation, which would false-RED this gate on
# changes that alter no suppression at all. Adding, removing or moving an
# annotation BETWEEN files still changes this file.
#
# Region: exactly the files the gate scans (`*.py` under `apps/*/src`, minus
# `test_*.py` / `*_test.py` / `conftest.py`) — Rule AL. An annotation outside
# that region is not honoured by the gate, so it is not counted here either.
#
# TO CHANGE THIS FILE: only in the same PR as the annotation you added or
# removed, with the reason visible in the diff. That is the entire point — this
# file is the review record for the suppression set. The gate prints a
# copy-pasteable replacement body when it fails.
#
# Current state: zero allowlisted captures repo-wide. The vocabulary exists and
# is documented in the gate header; nothing uses it yet.
count: 0
